course: dictionary
lesson: 13024
title: Formal words in context
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Facilitate» is a formal word. It means to make something easier, or to help it happen. «The new ramp facilitates access for wheelchairs.» The ramp makes it easier for wheelchairs to get in.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The ramp is new and it helps wheelchairs get in, so facilitate must mean make easier. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The new ramp makes access for wheelchairs easier.» It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Teachers often use facilitate for meetings and lessons: «The teacher will facilitate the discussion.» This means she guides it so that everyone can take part. In everyday talk, people usually say help or make easier instead.
fact: Facilitate is a verb: facilitate, facilitates, facilitated, facilitating.
fact: «Facilitate» means to make something easier or help it happen.
fact: «Facilitate» can also mean to guide a meeting or discussion so that everyone can take part.
fact: In science, enzymes facilitate reactions, which means they help the reactions happen.
fact: Formal words like «facilitate» are common in reports and exam questions. In everyday talk, «help» or «make easier» is usually used.
exercise: «The new ramp facilitates access for wheelchairs.» What does facilitates mean here? | Costs a lot of money | *Makes easier | Paints bright colours | Blocks completely
exercise: «The teacher will facilitate the discussion so everyone can speak.» What does facilitate mean here? | Read it aloud alone | Stop it quickly | *Guide it so everyone can take part | Write down every word in silence
exercise: In science, enzymes facilitate reactions. What does this tell you? | They change colour for no reason | They stop the reaction forever | *They help the reaction happen | They are a kind of food
test: «Our librarian facilitated the book club, so every child shared an opinion.» What does facilitated mean? | Cancelled it | *Helped it run smoothly | Forgot it | Painted it
test: Which word is closest in meaning to help or make easier? | forget | *facilitate | sprint | obey
exam: Read this: «The new lift facilitates access for everyone.» Which word is closest in meaning to facilitates? | Ignores | Hinders | Delays | *Helps
